            <ArticleTitle>Kawasaki disease--case reports and review of literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>666-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three cases of Kawasaki disease are described. One had coronary aneurysms detected by 2D Echogram. The pathogenesis and aetiology of Kawasaki disease are still unknown. Kawasaki disease is a clinical diagnosis made by exclusion and occurs mainly in infants and young children below the age of 5 years. Fever and at least 3 of the other 4 frequent features are essential for diagnosis. Acute cardiovascular complications vary from 30-60%, being mainly coronary artery aneurysms and thrombosis. Mortality rate is 1-2%. Aspirin is presently used.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
